    NIFRID:synonym "Lateral cutaneous nerve of the arm",
        "Nervus cutaneous brachii externus",
        "Nervus cutaneous brachii lateralis" ;
    definition: "The lateral brachial cutaneous nerve is a collective anatomical term for two distinct sensory nerves—the superior and inferior lateral brachial cutaneous nerves—that provide somatic sensation to the skin on the lateral (outer) aspect of the upper arm." ;
